Electronic Meeting 9 – 20 Nov 2020 Purpose: For information In order to assist RAN5 delegates to plan their submissions over the next 3 months, the deadlines that cover the period 23 Nov 2020 – 22 Feb 2021 are provided below: * It should be noted that company contributions (i.e. those not formally agreed at the WG) may be submitted directly to the RAN Plenary (independently of RAN5). I will present contributions on behalf of a company at the Plenary (wearing my Chair hat) if requested. The benefit of uploading documents on time is to ensure that interested parties have a reasonable time (a minimum of 5 working days for a regular meeting) to review the documents prior to the start of the RAN5 meeting. This is especially important for CRs that require a verdict at the meeting. Late docs may still be uploaded to the reflector but whilst tolerance is often shown by delegates, such documents may be deferred if more time is requested. It should also be noted that delegates must take care to select the correct agenda item, Work Item Code, TS version number when using the 3GU. Failure to do so creates nugatory work for the Secretary and wastes meeting time. It may also mean that documents could be presented for approval at the Plenary incorrectly with the possibility that such documents are rejected. [Tables] Table 1: 27 Nov 20 Fri | Deadline for WI rapporteurs to reserve Tdocs for WI Status Reports to RP#90-e ends 22:00 hrs UTC no later than 30 Nov 20 Mon | WI status reports to be submitted by 2200 hrs UTC (WI Rapporteurs) 14 Dec 20 Mon | Notification of RAN5 CR & WI proposal outcomes – post Plenary (RAN5 Chair) no later than 8 Jan 21 Fri | All draft specs (post Plenary) to be available for initial checking (RAN5 Sec) no later than 15 Jan 21 Fri | First draft agenda for RAN5#90-e to be distributed and 3GU opened (RAN5 Chair) 8 Feb 21 Mon | Deadline for reserving Tdocs for RAN5#90-e from the 3GU – 2000 hrs UTC 8 Feb 21 Mon | Deadline for uploading ‘in time’ RAN5#90-e Tdocs 